    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests the US_ENGLISH_GENEALOGY variant of Soundex encoding. Unlike the standard US_ENGLISH variant, this variant treats vowels (A, E, I, O, U, Y), H, and W as completely silent letters — they are ignored and do NOT act as separators between consonants with the same code. This produces encodings consistent with the genealogy research rules described at: http://www.genealogy.com/articles/research/00000060.html"
   },
   {
