    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     34,
     37
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "--- Vowels are silent (not separators) --- In standard Soundex, a vowel between two consonants with the same code keeps both consonants encoded. In the genealogy variant, the 'o' in \"Dodds\" is silent, so both 'd' sounds collapse to a single code: D200."
   },
   {
    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
